{"type":"message","id":"06c26e60","parentId":"460a2fc1","timestamp":"2026-02-18T11:24:22.230Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-02-18 16:54 GMT+5:30] URGENT: Investigate why OpenClaw gateway is flickering/restarting in a loop.\n\nContext:\n- We deleted a scheduled task named \"OpenClaw Gateway\" that was running `openclaw gateway restart` repeatedly.\n- After deletion, the flicker stopped temporarily, but it started again.\n- WhatsApp plugin was just enabled via config.patch. That triggered a restart, which is normal, but now something is causing repeated restarts.\n- There is NO gateway log file at D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\logs\\gateway.log (it's missing or empty).\n- Flicker appears as console windows opening/closing repeatedly.\n\nYour mission:\n1. Check for any remaining scheduled tasks that might be restarting the gateway (use `schtasks /query /fo LIST /v` and look for OpenClaw/gateway).\n2. Check the Startup folder (`shell:startup`) for any shortcuts/scripts.\n3. Check if any processes are listening on port 18789 (`netstat -an | findstr :18789`).\n4. Look for any lingering `node.exe` processes that could be the gateway.\n5. Examine the workspace for any batch files or scripts that might be launching the gateway (search for \"openclaw\" or \"gateway\" in .bat/.cmd files).\n6. Check if the gateway binary exists and is runnable (`where openclaw`).\n7. Determine what is spawning new console windows (process monitor approach: watch for new `cmd.exe` or `openclaw.exe` processes launching).\n8. Provide a clear diagnosis and recommended fix to stop the loop.\n\nReturn a concise report with:\n- What you found\n- Root cause\n- Exact steps to fix it\n- Whether the Windows service installation files we created are ready to use (scripts/gateway-wrapper.bat, scripts/install-service.bat exist?)"}],"timestamp":1771413862229}}
